IMPORT prelude

-- Motor Vehicle (Third Party Insurance) Act 1943 (Western Australia) -- compulsory third party (CTP) insurance, from the
-- seat of the vehicle owner and of the person injured by a vehicle.
--
-- SEAT: the vehicle owner ("What does my compulsory third party insurance cover, the policy that comes with licensing the
-- vehicle?") and the person injured by a motor vehicle ("Whom do I claim against? What notice must I give, and when? What if
-- the vehicle was uninsured or never identified? Am I covered riding an e-bike or eRideable?"). Every exported question is
-- phrased as one of them would ask it. What the Act tells the Insurance Commission, the Director General, a court or the
-- police to do is encoded only as what it means for that person: what may be done to them, what they must be given, and by
-- when.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 3(1) (motor vehicle, owner, insured person, uninsured motor vehicle), s 3(3), (3A), (4), (6), (7)
-- (Crown vehicles, visiting vehicles, defence use, "caused by a vehicle"); ss 3C, 3D, 3F, 3FB (the restrictions on damages:
-- non-pecuniary loss, gratuitous care, earning capacity, no contributory-negligence deduction for catastrophic care); s 3G
-- (an employer-owner liable for workers' compensation); s 4(1), (3A)-(3C), (4), (5), (5A), (7A)-(7C), (8), (8A), (9), (10)
-- (the compulsory policy, the offence of using an uninsured vehicle, the policy that comes with the licence); s 6(1) and the
-- Schedule (what the policy covers, its warranties and conditions); s 6A (catastrophic injury: CISS payments only); s 7
-- (claims against an insured person or the Commission, the dead or unservable insured, the unidentified vehicle, no defence
-- for breach, recovery from the insured); s 8 (uninsured vehicles); s 10 (notice of the accident; no admission or settlement
-- without consent); s 12 (emergency treatment and conveyance); s 15 (unauthorised drivers); s 19 (no early termination);
-- s 20 (the policy follows the vehicle); s 21 (the 15 days after a licence expires); s 22 (an employee's own vehicle used
-- for the employer); s 26 (no contracting out); s 27A (legal costs); s 29 (notice of claim; the Commission's application);
-- s 29A (leave to proceed); s 30 (medical examination).
--
-- Edition: the Motor Vehicle (Third Party Insurance) Act 1943 (No. 32 of 1943) as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_47506.txt (legislation.wa.gov.au mrdoc 47506, retrieved 2026-09-07); its compilation
-- table runs to the Workers Compensation and Injury Management Act 2023 (No. 21 of 2023), in operation 1 July 2024. The
-- Motor Vehicle (Third Party Insurance) Regulations 2009, version 00-d0-00, currency start 1 July 2024, as deposited at
-- ../../../motor-vehicle-third-party-insurance-regulations-2009/registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_47391.txt (retrieved
-- 2026-10-19), used for: the prescribed notice of claim (r 5(1), Schedule 1); permits and plates that carry a policy
-- (rr 8, 9, 10); the licence as evidence of cover (r 11).
--
-- NUMBERS THAT ARE INPUTS. The regulations set NO premium: the premium is "determined by the Commission" (s 4(8)) and
-- approved by the Minister (s 3T), so it is not encoded. Amounts A, B, C (s 3C) and D (s 3D) are recalculated every 1 July
-- and gazetted; the deposit's note 1 tables them only up to 1 July 2010 ($337 000, $17 000, $51 000, $6 000), so they are
-- inputs. The average weekly earnings figures (ss 3D(3), 3F(5)) are the Australian Statistician's, so they are inputs.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the formula in s 3C(6) (the damages for non-pecuniary loss assessed between Amount C and Amounts B and C
-- together): the deposit shows the words "the excess of the amount so assessed over --" and then nothing, the formula
-- having been an image; that band answers NOTHING. The formula in r 6(b) for paying a person who conveys the injured
-- person is missing for the same reason (only P, D and R are defined), so the conveyor's amount is not computed. Also not
-- encoded: s 3EA (CISS interim participants), s 3FA (awards in other jurisdictions), ss 3Q-3T (the Director General and
-- the Commission's administration), s 11 (the Commission's conduct of claims) beyond its effect in s 10(5), s 14 (recovery
-- of emergency payments from an uninsured owner), s 16 (jurisdiction and periodical payments), s 17 (temporary licences for
-- visitors), s 18 (disqualification on application), ss 23-25, 27, 27B, 27C, 28, 33, 34, the MVWA(CI) Act itself (whether
-- an injury is "catastrophic" is asked as a fact), and the Road Traffic (Vehicles) Act 2012 (whether a vehicle "is required
-- to be licensed" is asked as a fact).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the seat of the vehicle owner and the injured person,
-- with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate.
-- Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.
--
-- Conventions. Money is in dollars. Periods are in the unit the name says (days, months, weeks, hours).

§ `Motor Vehicle (Third Party Insurance) Act 1943 -- the owner and the injured person`

§§ `Arithmetic`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER
      `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER
      `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `s 3(1), (3), (4), (6), s 4(9), (10) -- is my vehicle a "motor vehicle", and must it be insured`

-- s 3(1): "motor vehicle means any vehicle propelled by gas, oil, electricity or any other motive power, not being animal
-- power, required to be licensed, and complying with the requirements necessary for licensing, under the Vehicles Act and
-- includes a caravan, trailer or semitrailer drawn or hauled by a motor vehicle".
-- Gloss: a powered vehicle that the Road Traffic (Vehicles) Act 2012 requires to be licensed, plus anything it tows.
-- The Act does not mention bicycles, e-bikes or eRideables. Whether one "is required to be licensed" under the Vehicles Act
-- is a borrowed term, asked as a fact: an electric vehicle that is not required to be licensed is not a "motor vehicle" here.
-- s 4(9), (10): the Director General must, when required, issue a policy for a powered vehicle that does not need a licence
-- but complies with the licensing requirements, and its owner and driver then have "the same rights" and "the same duties
-- and obligations" as if it were a motor vehicle.
DECLARE `What drives it` IS ONE OF
    `an engine or an electric motor`      -- "gas, oil, electricity or any other motive power"
    `pedals or animal power only`
    `nothing of its own (it is towed)`

DECLARE `My vehicle` HAS
    `what drives it`                                                     IS A `What drives it`
    `it is required to be licensed under the Vehicles Act`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `it complies with the requirements for licensing`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a caravan, trailer or semitrailer drawn by a motor vehicle`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `a policy was issued for it under s 4(9)`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is on a road`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is owned by the Crown and used solely in public business`        IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 3(3)
    `it is visiting, licensed in a prescribed State and insured there`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 3(4), (4B)
    `it is commandeered or used for defence purposes`                    IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 3(6)

GIVEN `the vehicle` IS A `My vehicle`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a motor vehicle under s 3` IF
        `the vehicle`'s `it is a caravan, trailer or semitrailer drawn by a motor vehicle`
    OR (    `the vehicle`'s `what drives it` EQUALS `an engine or an electric motor`
        AND `the vehicle`'s `it is required to be licensed under the Vehicles Act`
        AND `the vehicle`'s `it complies with the requirements for licensing`)

@export Is my vehicle a "motor vehicle" under the Motor Vehicle (Third Party Insurance) Act 1943 (WA) (s 3(1), s 4(10))?
GIVEN `the vehicle` IS A `My vehicle` @desc What drives your vehicle, whether the Road Traffic (Vehicles) Act requires it to be licensed, and whether a policy was issued for it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my vehicle a motor vehicle under the Act` IF
        `is a motor vehicle under s 3` `the vehicle`
    OR (    `the vehicle`'s `what drives it` EQUALS `an engine or an electric motor`
        AND `the vehicle`'s `it complies with the requirements for licensing`
        AND `the vehicle`'s `a policy was issued for it under s 4(9)`)

-- s 4(1): "When any motor vehicle is on a road there is required to be in force in relation to the motor vehicle a contract
-- of insurance entered into by the owner". Not obligatory for a Crown vehicle "used solely in the public business" (s 3(3));
-- not necessary for a vehicle "temporarily in this State" licensed in a prescribed State whose owner and driver are insured
-- under that State's law (s 3(4)); the Act "shall cease to have any effect" for a vehicle commandeered or used for defence
-- purposes (s 3(6)).
@export Must my vehicle be covered by compulsory third party insurance (s 4(1), s 3(3), (4), (6))?
GIVEN `the vehicle` IS A `My vehicle` @desc Your vehicle, whether it is on a road, and whether it is a Crown, visiting or defence vehicle
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my vehicle be insured` IF
        `is a motor vehicle under s 3` `the vehicle`
    AND `the vehicle`'s `it is on a road`
    AND (NOT `the vehicle`'s `it is owned by the Crown and used solely in public business`)
    AND (NOT `the vehicle`'s `it is visiting, licensed in a prescribed State and insured there`)
    AND (NOT `the vehicle`'s `it is commandeered or used for defence purposes`)

-- The rider's question, as far as the text goes: an e-bike or eRideable is covered by a policy under this Act only if it
-- is a "motor vehicle" (it must be licensed under the Vehicles Act) or a policy was issued for it under s 4(9). The Act
-- says nothing else about them. Whether the rider is covered when HURT by a car is the injured person's question below.
@export Does compulsory third party insurance cover injuries caused by my e-bike or eRideable (s 3(1), s 4(9), (10))?
GIVEN `the vehicle` IS A `My vehicle` @desc Your e-bike or eRideable: what drives it, whether the Road Traffic (Vehicles) Act requires it to be licensed and whether it is licensed or a policy was issued for it
      `it is licensed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a vehicle licence is in force for it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does CTP cover injuries caused by my e-bike or eRideable` IF
        (`is a motor vehicle under s 3` `the vehicle` AND `it is licensed`)
    OR `the vehicle`'s `a policy was issued for it under s 4(9)`

§§ `s 3(1) -- am I an "owner"`

-- s 3(1): "owner when used in relation to a motor vehicle which is the subject of a hire purchase agreement means the person
-- in possession of that vehicle under that agreement; and ... a hiring agreement ... includes any persons who have hired the
-- vehicle ... Save as aforesaid the term owner means and includes every person who is the owner or part owner or joint owner
-- ..., but does not include the grantee under a Bill of Sale by way of security ... except when such grantee takes
-- possession ... by way of enforcing his rights".
DECLARE `How I hold the vehicle` IS ONE OF
    `I own it, alone, in part or jointly`
    `I have it under a hire purchase agreement`
    `I have hired it`
    `I let it out under a hire purchase agreement`
    `I hold a bill of sale over it as security`
    `I hold a bill of sale over it and have taken possession to enforce it`

@export Am I the "owner" of the vehicle for compulsory third party insurance (s 3(1))?
GIVEN `how` IS A `How I hold the vehicle` @desc How you hold the vehicle
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I an owner under the Act` IF
    CONSIDER `how`
    WHEN `I let it out under a hire purchase agreement` THEN FALSE    -- the owner is "the person in possession"
    WHEN `I hold a bill of sale over it as security` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `s 4(8), (8A), s 20, s 21, rr 8-11 -- is a policy in force for my vehicle`

-- s 4(8): "no licence is to be granted or renewed ... unless ... there is paid to and received by the Director General the
-- appropriate insurance premium determined by the Commission". s 4(8A): "The grant or renewal of a licence ... is to be
-- taken to constitute the issue of a policy of insurance complying with this Act -- (a) in respect of the motor vehicle;
-- and (b) in respect of the period for which the licence is granted or renewed." r 11: the licence "is evidence that a
-- policy ... has been issued".
-- s 21(2): renewed "within the period of 15 days after the day on which the vehicle licence expired", the policy is
-- "extended until the vehicle licence is renewed". (4): renewed later, "the motor vehicle is an uninsured motor vehicle for
-- the period beginning on the day after the day on which the vehicle licence expired and ending on the day on which the
-- vehicle licence is renewed". (5): the premium is unaffected.
-- rr 8, 9: a permit for an unlicensed vehicle, or plates for use on one, may incorporate or be issued with a policy;
-- r 10: otherwise no policy for an unlicensed vehicle without the managing director's approval.
DECLARE `Licence status` IS ONE OF
    `the vehicle licence is current`
    `the vehicle licence has expired`
    `unlicensed, on a permit or plates issued with a policy (rr 8, 9)`
    `unlicensed, and no policy was issued`

DECLARE `My licence` HAS
    `status`                                         IS A `Licence status`
    `it has been renewed since it expired`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `days after expiry that it was or will be renewed, or that have passed` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `My cover` IS ONE OF
    `covered by the policy that came with the licence (s 4(8A))`
    `covered: the policy is extended until the renewal (s 21(2))`
    `covered only if the licence is renewed within 15 days after it expired (s 21(2))`
    `not covered: an uninsured motor vehicle from the day after expiry until renewal (s 21(4))`
    `covered by a policy issued with a permit or plates (rr 8, 9)`
    `not covered: no policy has been issued`

`the days of grace after a licence expires` MEANS 15

@export Is my vehicle covered by compulsory third party insurance right now (s 4(8A), s 21, rr 8-11)?
GIVEN `the licence` IS A `My licence` @desc Whether the vehicle licence is current or has expired, and if expired, whether and how many days after expiry it was renewed (or how many days have passed)
GIVETH A `My cover`
DECIDE `Is my vehicle covered` IS
    CONSIDER `the licence`'s `status`
    WHEN `the vehicle licence is current` THEN `covered by the policy that came with the licence (s 4(8A))`
    WHEN `unlicensed, on a permit or plates issued with a policy (rr 8, 9)` THEN `covered by a policy issued with a permit or plates (rr 8, 9)`
    WHEN `unlicensed, and no policy was issued` THEN `not covered: no policy has been issued`
    WHEN `the vehicle licence has expired` THEN
        IF `the licence`'s `days after expiry that it was or will be renewed, or that have passed` GREATER THAN `the days of grace after a licence expires`
        THEN `not covered: an uninsured motor vehicle from the day after expiry until renewal (s 21(4))`
        ELSE IF `the licence`'s `it has been renewed since it expired`
             THEN `covered: the policy is extended until the renewal (s 21(2))`
             ELSE `covered only if the licence is renewed within 15 days after it expired (s 21(2))`

@export Can my vehicle licence be granted or renewed without paying the compulsory third party premium (s 4(8))?
GIVEN `the premium has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurance premium determined by the Insurance Commission has been paid to the Director General
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my vehicle licence be granted or renewed` IF `the premium has been paid`

-- s 20(1): the policy "shall not be deemed to be cancelled ... solely by reason of a change of ownership" and "shall ...
-- enure in favour of every person who, during the period for which the policy was granted or renewed, becomes an owner";
-- (2) every such owner is bound by its terms "as if he had expressly agreed to them".
@export If I buy a licensed vehicle, does its compulsory third party policy carry on for me (s 20)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the policy carry on for me when I buy the vehicle` IS TRUE

-- s 19: "The Commission shall not terminate a policy ... before its expiry by effluxion of time, except in cases where the
-- motor vehicle concerned is no longer required to be insured under this Act."
@export May the Insurance Commission end my compulsory third party policy before it expires (s 19)?
GIVEN `the vehicle no longer needs to be insured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle is no longer required to be insured under the Act
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Commission end my policy early` IF `the vehicle no longer needs to be insured`

§§ `s 6(1), the Schedule, s 3(7), s 3G -- what does my policy cover`

-- s 6(1)(b): the policy must "insure the owner of the vehicle ... and any other person who at any time drives that vehicle,
-- whether with or without the consent of the owner, in respect of all liability for negligence which may be incurred by
-- that owner or other person in respect of the death of or bodily injury to any person directly caused by, or by the
-- driving of, the vehicle in any part of the Commonwealth". The Schedule form says the same, for the licence period.
-- s 3(7): death or injury "shall not be taken to have been caused by a vehicle if it is not a consequence of the driving of
-- that vehicle or of the vehicle running out of control". Whether a harm (a door opened into a passing rider, say) was a
-- consequence of "the driving" is a court's judgment: an input.
-- s 3G: if the owner is liable as an employer under the Workers Compensation and Injury Management Act 2023 for the death
-- or injury, neither the Act nor the policy applies to the owner's negligence "other than liability for the negligent
-- driving of the motor vehicle".
-- Property damage is not covered: the policy is against liability for death or bodily injury only (s 6(1)(b); s 11(3)
-- speaks of a person "insured against his liability for death or bodily injury but not against his liability for damage to
-- property").
DECLARE `The harm` IS ONE OF
    `the death of a person`
    `bodily injury to a person`
    `damage to a vehicle or other property only`

DECLARE `The incident` HAS
    `the harm`                                                       IS A `The harm`
    `a policy was in force for the vehicle`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person liable is the owner or someone driving the vehicle`  IS A BOOLEAN   -- with or without the owner's consent
    `the liability is for negligence`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was a consequence of the driving or of the vehicle running out of control` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 3(7)
    `it happened in Australia`                                       IS A BOOLEAN   -- "any part of the Commonwealth"
    `the owner is liable for it as an employer under workers' compensation` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 3G(1)
    `the liability is for the negligent driving of the vehicle`      IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 3G(2)

@export Does my compulsory third party policy cover this liability (s 6(1)(b), Schedule, s 3(7), s 3G)?
GIVEN `the incident` IS AN `The incident` @desc What harm was done, who is liable and for what, where, and whether the policy was in force
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my policy cover this liability` IF
        `the incident`'s `a policy was in force for the vehicle`
    AND (NOT (`the incident`'s `the harm` EQUALS `damage to a vehicle or other property only`))
    AND `the incident`'s `the person liable is the owner or someone driving the vehicle`
    AND `the incident`'s `the liability is for negligence`
    AND `the incident`'s `it was a consequence of the driving or of the vehicle running out of control`
    AND `the incident`'s `it happened in Australia`
    AND (   (NOT `the incident`'s `the owner is liable for it as an employer under workers' compensation`)
         OR `the incident`'s `the liability is for the negligent driving of the vehicle`)

-- s 6A(2): a policy "is also taken to insure any person (the injured person) against the risk of suffering a catastrophic
-- injury that -- (a) is a motor vehicle injury to which the MVWA(CI) Act applies; and (b) results from a motor vehicle
-- accident involving the vehicle mentioned in the policy." (3): it "extends only to the making of payments under the CISS"
-- for "necessary and reasonable expenses" for "assessed treatment, care and support needs". No fault is required, so the
-- driver at fault is covered too. Whether the injury is "catastrophic" and within that Act is asked as a fact.
@export If I am catastrophically injured in an accident involving my vehicle, does my policy cover me, even if it was my fault (s 6A)?
GIVEN `the injury is catastrophic under the MVWA(CI) Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury is a catastrophic injury under the Motor Vehicle and Workplace Accidents (Catastrophic Injuries) Act 2016
      `that Act applies to it as a motor vehicle injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a motor vehicle injury to which that Act applies
      `the accident involved the insured vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accident involved the vehicle named in the policy
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I covered for CISS payments for a catastrophic injury` IF
        `the injury is catastrophic under the MVWA(CI) Act`
    AND `that Act applies to it as a motor vehicle injury`
    AND `the accident involved the insured vehicle`

-- s 22(1): an owner who uses an insured vehicle in the employer's service, with the employer's acquiescence -- the policy
-- "shall ... enure in favour of the employer as well as of the owner". (2): used "without the knowledge or contrary to the
-- instructions of the employer, the employer shall not in any manner whatsoever be liable" to a person injured by it.
DECLARE `My employer and my car` IS ONE OF
    `I use it for work and my employer acquiesces`
    `I use it for work without my employer's knowledge or against instructions`
    `I do not use it for work`

DECLARE `Where my employer stands` IS ONE OF
    `my policy covers my employer as if an owner (s 22(1))`
    `my employer is not liable at all to a person injured while I so use it (s 22(2))`
    `s 22 does not apply`

@export Does my compulsory third party policy cover my employer when I use my own car for work (s 22)?
GIVEN `use` IS A `My employer and my car` @desc Whether you use your car for your employer's work, and on what terms
GIVETH A `Where my employer stands`
DECIDE `Where does my employer stand` IS
    CONSIDER `use`
    WHEN `I use it for work and my employer acquiesces` THEN `my policy covers my employer as if an owner (s 22(1))`
    WHEN `I use it for work without my employer's knowledge or against instructions` THEN `my employer is not liable at all to a person injured while I so use it (s 22(2))`
    WHEN `I do not use it for work` THEN `s 22 does not apply`

§§ `s 7(4), (5), s 10(6), s 15, Schedule -- can the Commission make me repay`

-- Schedule, warranties: the owner warrants the vehicle will not be "(a) used for any other purpose than that stated ...;
-- (b) driven in an unsafe or damaged condition; (c) driven by or in charge of himself or any other person who is
-- unlicensed to drive or who is under the influence of intoxicating liquor", with a defence to (c) if the owner proves it
-- was so driven "without his knowledge or consent".
-- s 7(4): none of these is a defence against the injured person. s 7(5): the Commission "may ... recover from the insured
-- person liable ..., and from the owner where the insured person liable ... is not the owner ... and at the time of the
-- accident the owner was guilty of any of the matters". s 15: a driver "without the authority of the owner or without
-- reasonable grounds for believing that he had the authority" gets no indemnity and must repay. s 10(6): the Commission
-- may recover from "any person who has failed to comply with any provision of this section".
-- The s 7(5) proviso (an unreasonable refusal of the insured's written request to settle caps what may be recovered) is
-- not encoded.
DECLARE `My part in the accident` IS ONE OF
    `I was driving, and I am liable`
    `I own the vehicle, and someone else was driving`

DECLARE `What went wrong` HAS
    `there was a misstatement or nondisclosure when the policy was obtained`      IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 7(4)(a)
    `a term, warranty or condition of the policy, or the Act, was breached`        IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 7(4)(b), e.g. a drunk or unlicensed driver
    `a condition about what to do after the accident was not complied with`       IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 7(4)(c)
    `I was myself guilty of that matter`                                          IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 7(5), the owner; the warranty (c) defence
    `the driver had no authority and no reasonable grounds to believe he had`     IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 15
    `I failed to give a notice or keep a duty under s 10`                         IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 10(6)

@export Can the Insurance Commission make me repay what it paid the injured person (s 7(5), s 10(6), s 15, Schedule)?
GIVEN `my part` IS A `My part in the accident` @desc Whether you were the liable driver or the owner when someone else drove
      `what went wrong` IS A `What went wrong` @desc Misstatements, breaches of the policy's warranties or conditions, unauthorised driving and missed notices
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Commission make me repay` IF
    CONSIDER `my part`
    WHEN `I was driving, and I am liable` THEN
            `a section 7(4) matter arose` `what went wrong`
         OR `what went wrong`'s `the driver had no authority and no reasonable grounds to believe he had`
         OR `what went wrong`'s `I failed to give a notice or keep a duty under s 10`
    WHEN `I own the vehicle, and someone else was driving` THEN
            (`a section 7(4) matter arose` `what went wrong` AND `what went wrong`'s `I was myself guilty of that matter`)
         OR `what went wrong`'s `I failed to give a notice or keep a duty under s 10`

GIVEN `w` IS A `What went wrong`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a section 7(4) matter arose` IF
        `w`'s `there was a misstatement or nondisclosure when the policy was obtained`
    OR `w`'s `a term, warranty or condition of the policy, or the Act, was breached`
    OR `w`'s `a condition about what to do after the accident was not complied with`

-- s 7(4): "It shall be no defence by the Commission to an action against it ... that it is not liable under a policy ... by
-- reason of" misstatement, breach, or failure to comply after the event. The injured person is paid all the same.
@export If the driver was drunk or unlicensed, or the owner misled the insurer, can the Commission refuse to pay me (s 7(4))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Commission refuse to pay me because of a breach of the policy` IS FALSE

§§ `s 10 -- what I must do after an accident`

-- s 10(1): on an accident resulting in death or bodily injury "directly caused by, or by the driving of, an insured or an
-- uninsured motor vehicle, the driver and the person in charge thereof shall give written notice forthwith to the
-- Commission" of the fact, time and place, circumstances, the injured and the witnesses. (2): if neither is the owner, "the
-- owner ... shall give a like notice immediately upon the accident coming to his knowledge". (4): failing to comply with
-- (1) or (3) is an offence, "Penalty: $20". The approved forms are listed in r 5(2).
DECLARE `My role` IS ONE OF
    `the driver or person in charge of the vehicle`
    `the owner, not driving or in charge`
    `the injured person`
    `a passenger or witness`

DECLARE `Notice of the accident` IS ONE OF
    `written notice to the Insurance Commission forthwith (s 10(1))`
    `written notice to the Insurance Commission immediately on learning of the accident (s 10(2))`
    `no notice of the accident is required of me by s 10`

@export Must I give the Insurance Commission written notice of the accident, and when (s 10(1), (2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A `My role` @desc Your part in the accident
      `someone was killed or injured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accident killed or injured anyone
      `it was caused by a motor vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was directly caused by, or by the driving of, a motor vehicle (insured or not)
GIVETH A `Notice of the accident`
DECIDE `Must I give notice of the accident` IS
    IF (NOT (`someone was killed or injured` AND `it was caused by a motor vehicle`))
    THEN `no notice of the accident is required of me by s 10`
    ELSE CONSIDER `my role`
         WHEN `the driver or person in charge of the vehicle` THEN `written notice to the Insurance Commission forthwith (s 10(1))`
         WHEN `the owner, not driving or in charge` THEN `written notice to the Insurance Commission immediately on learning of the accident (s 10(2))`
         OTHERWISE `no notice of the accident is required of me by s 10`

@export What is the most I can be fined for not giving the Insurance Commission notice of an accident or a claim (s 10(4))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined for not giving notice` IS 20

-- s 10(5): an insured person, and the owner and driver of an uninsured vehicle, "shall not, without the consent in writing
-- of the Commission -- (a) enter upon or incur any expense in any litigation; (b) make any offer or promise of payment or
-- settlement; (c) make any payment or settlement; or (d) make any admission of liability ... but this provision shall not
-- prevent any person truthfully answering any questions reasonably asked of him."
DECLARE `What I want to do` IS ONE OF
    `admit liability`
    `offer or promise to pay or settle`
    `pay or settle`
    `start or spend money on litigation`
    `answer truthfully a question reasonably asked of me`

@export May I do this about the accident without the Insurance Commission's written consent (s 10(5))?
GIVEN `the act` IS A `What I want to do` @desc What you want to do about the claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I do it without the Commission's consent` IF
    `the act` EQUALS `answer truthfully a question reasonably asked of me`

§§ `s 4(3A)-(7C) -- what happens if I use my vehicle uninsured`

-- s 4(3A): a vehicle without a complying policy "used on a road" -- "the owner ... and any person so using the motor vehicle
-- or causing or permitting such use commits an offence. Penalty: First offence: $400. Subsequent offence: $800."
@export What is the most I can be fined for using my vehicle on a road uninsured (s 4(3A))?
GIVEN `I have been convicted of it before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this is a second or later offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined for using my vehicle uninsured` IS
    IF `I have been convicted of it before` THEN 800 ELSE 400

-- s 4(4): a person convicted "shall (unless the court thinks fit to order otherwise) be disqualified from holding and
-- obtaining ... a driver's licence or ... a licence in respect of a motor vehicle for a period of 12 months". The court's
-- choice is an input.
@export For how many months will I lose my driver's licence and vehicle licence if convicted of using my vehicle uninsured (s 4(4))?
GIVEN `the court orders otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court thinks fit to order otherwise
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `For how many months am I disqualified` IS
    IF `the court orders otherwise` THEN 0 ELSE 12

-- s 4(3C): if the owner held no vehicle licence, the court "shall order the person convicted ... to pay the amount of the
-- annual licence fee that should have been paid".
@export Must I also pay the annual licence fee if convicted of using an unlicensed, uninsured vehicle (s 4(3C))?
GIVEN `the owner held the vehicle licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the owner held the vehicle licence the Road Traffic (Vehicles) Act requires
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I also pay the licence fee` IF (NOT `the owner held the vehicle licence`)

-- s 4(3B): no conviction or punishment under (3A) if already convicted or acquitted of, or paid an infringement notice for,
-- an offence under the Vehicles Act s 4(2) "and both those offences had been committed simultaneously".
@export Can I be punished for using my vehicle uninsured when I have already been dealt with for driving it unlicensed (s 4(3B))?
GIVEN `already dealt with for the Vehicles Act s 4(2) offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been convicted or acquitted of, or paid an infringement notice for, the Road Traffic (Vehicles) Act s 4(2) offence
      `both offences were committed at the same time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether both offences were committed simultaneously
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be punished for uninsured use as well` IF
    (NOT (`already dealt with for the Vehicles Act s 4(2) offence` AND `both offences were committed at the same time`))

-- s 4(5): proceedings "within a period of 6 months from the date of the commission ... or ... within a period of 3 months
-- from the date on which it came to the knowledge of the prosecutor ..., whichever period is the longer"; (5A): never "after
-- the expiration of one year from the date of the commission".
@export Up to how many months after the offence can I be prosecuted for using my vehicle uninsured (s 4(5), (5A))?
GIVEN `months after the offence that the prosecutor learned of it` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months after the offence the prosecutor learned of it
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Up to how many months after the offence can I be prosecuted` IS
    `the lesser of` 12 (`the greater of` 6 (`months after the offence that the prosecutor learned of it` PLUS 3))

-- s 4(7A): an owner must, on a police officer's request, produce evidence of a complying policy for every vehicle owned;
-- (7B) complied with if produced "at a Police Station (to be nominated by the owner ...) within 5 days"; (7C) failing
-- "without just excuse" is an offence, "Penalty: $200".
@export Have I complied with a police request to show my vehicle is insured (s 4(7A)-(7C))?
GIVEN `I produced the evidence when asked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you produced evidence of insurance when the police officer asked
      `days until I produced it at the police station I nominated` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days after the request you produced it at the police station you nominated (0 if not produced)
      `I produced it at the nominated station` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you produced it at the police station you nominated
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I complied with the request to produce evidence of insurance` IF
        `I produced the evidence when asked`
    OR (`I produced it at the nominated station` AND `days until I produced it at the police station I nominated` AT MOST 5)

@export What is the most I can be fined for failing, without just excuse, to produce evidence of insurance (s 4(7C))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined for not producing evidence of insurance` IS 200

§§ `ss 7, 8, 3(3A), 3(1) "uninsured motor vehicle" -- whom do I claim against`

-- The injured person's question. The claim is for negligence: the policy covers "all liability for negligence" (s 6(1)(b)),
-- and ss 7(2), (3) speak of death or injury caused "by negligence". With no negligent party there is no claim under the
-- Act, save the no-fault CISS cover for a catastrophic injury (s 6A, above).
-- s 7(1): a person "who has obtained a judgment against an insured person" may recover the unsatisfied part from the
-- Commission; with s 11 the Commission conducts and pays the claim. "Insured person" (s 3(1)): the owner of an insured
-- vehicle "and the driver at the material time whether with or without the consent of the owner".
-- s 7(2): if the insured person "is dead or cannot be served with process", action against the Commission, on notice.
-- s 7(3): if "the identity of the vehicle cannot be ascertained", action against the Commission, provided the claimant
-- "made due search and inquiry" and gave written notice "as soon as practicable after the happening of the accident".
-- s 8(1): judgment against the owner or driver of an uninsured motor vehicle, unpaid in full "within one month", may be
-- claimed from the Commission. s 8(5): if that owner or driver "is dead or cannot after strict inquiry and search be found",
-- judgment against the Commission.
-- s 3(1): an "uninsured motor vehicle" is one required to be insured and not; "The expression does not include a motor
-- vehicle owned by the Commonwealth". A visiting vehicle within s 3(4) is not required to be insured here, so it is not
-- "uninsured" either: the Act gives no claim on the Commission for it (the encoder's reading; the claim lies against its
-- owner or driver, whose home-State insurance s 3(4) presupposes).
-- s 3(3A): an uninsured State vehicle -- "the Crown shall be under the same liabilities ... as an insurer".
DECLARE `The vehicle that hurt me` IS ONE OF
    `a vehicle insured under this Act`                 -- licensed in WA, or otherwise covered
    `an uninsured motor vehicle`
    `a Commonwealth vehicle`
    `a State vehicle that is not insured`
    `a visiting vehicle insured under its own State's law`
    `a vehicle that has not been identified`
    `not a motor vehicle under this Act`               -- a bicycle; an e-bike or eRideable not required to be licensed

DECLARE `What happened to me` HAS
    `the vehicle`                                       IS A `The vehicle that hurt me`
    `it was a consequence of the driving or of the vehicle running out of control` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 3(7)
    `the driver or owner was negligent`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person at fault is dead or cannot be found or served` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Whom I claim against` IS ONE OF
    `the owner or driver, as an insured person; the Insurance Commission conducts and pays the claim (ss 7(1), 11)`
    `the Insurance Commission directly, for what I could have recovered from the insured person (s 7(2))`
    `the Insurance Commission directly, if I made due search and inquiry and gave notice (s 7(3))`
    `the owner or driver; if the judgment is unpaid after one month, the Insurance Commission (s 8(1))`
    `the Insurance Commission directly, for what I could have recovered from the owner or driver (s 8(5))`
    `the owner or driver; the State answers as an insurer would (s 3(3A))`
    `the owner or driver under the general law; this Act gives no claim on the Commission`
    `no claim under this Act`

@export I was hurt by a vehicle: whom do I claim against (ss 7, 8, 3(1), 3(3A), 3(7))?
GIVEN `what happened` IS A `What happened to me` @desc The vehicle that hurt you, whether the harm came from its driving or its running out of control, whether someone was negligent, and whether that person is dead or cannot be found or served
GIVETH A `Whom I claim against`
DECIDE `Whom do I claim against` IS
    IF (NOT (    `what happened`'s `it was a consequence of the driving or of the vehicle running out of control`
             AND `what happened`'s `the driver or owner was negligent`))
    THEN `no claim under this Act`
    ELSE CONSIDER `what happened`'s `the vehicle`
         WHEN `a vehicle insured under this Act` THEN
             IF `what happened`'s `the person at fault is dead or cannot be found or served`
             THEN `the Insurance Commission directly, for what I could have recovered from the insured person (s 7(2))`
             ELSE `the owner or driver, as an insured person; the Insurance Commission conducts and pays the claim (ss 7(1), 11)`
         WHEN `an uninsured motor vehicle` THEN
             IF `what happened`'s `the person at fault is dead or cannot be found or served`
             THEN `the Insurance Commission directly, for what I could have recovered from the owner or driver (s 8(5))`
             ELSE `the owner or driver; if the judgment is unpaid after one month, the Insurance Commission (s 8(1))`
         WHEN `a vehicle that has not been identified` THEN `the Insurance Commission directly, if I made due search and inquiry and gave notice (s 7(3))`
         WHEN `a State vehicle that is not insured` THEN `the owner or driver; the State answers as an insurer would (s 3(3A))`
         WHEN `a Commonwealth vehicle` THEN `the owner or driver under the general law; this Act gives no claim on the Commission`
         WHEN `a visiting vehicle insured under its own State's law` THEN `the owner or driver under the general law; this Act gives no claim on the Commission`
         WHEN `not a motor vehicle under this Act` THEN `no claim under this Act`

§§ `ss 29, 29A, 30, 7(2), 7(3), 8(6) -- notice of my claim, and what can bar it`

-- s 29(1): no action may be commenced or maintained "unless the person proposing to claim the damages ... has given to the
-- Commission, as soon as practicable after the occurrence giving rise to the claim, notice in writing prescribed by the
-- regulations of his intention to make the claim". r 5(1): the form in Schedule 1 ("NOTICE OF INTENTION TO MAKE CLAIM").
-- No fixed number of days: "as soon as practicable" is a judgment, asked as a fact.
-- ss 7(2), 8(6): notice to the Commission as soon as practicable after the claimant knew the person at fault was dead or
-- could not be served or found. s 7(3): due search and inquiry, and written notice, as soon as practicable after the accident.
-- s 29A: the court may relieve the failure or defect, or give leave to proceed, if it "was occasioned by mistake,
-- inadvertence or any other reasonable cause or ... the Commission is not materially prejudiced" -- the court's judgment,
-- an input.
-- s 30(5): refusing, without reasonable excuse, an examination by the Commission's health professional means "no action
-- for damages is to be commenced or proceeded with unless the injured person has undergone the examination".
-- s 29(7): if a judge has fixed a time to commence and it passes, the claim is "forever barred and extinguished".
-- For a claim on which the Act gives nothing (no claim, or a general-law claim against a Commonwealth or visiting vehicle)
-- these conditions do not apply: the first answers FALSE (there is nothing to bring), the second TRUE (the Act sets none).
DECLARE `My claim steps` HAS
    `I gave the prescribed notice of intention to claim as soon as practicable`       IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 29(1), r 5(1)
    `I made due search and inquiry for the vehicle as soon as practicable`             IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 7(3)(a)
    `I gave written notice of the claim as soon as practicable after the accident`     IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 7(3)(b)
    `I gave notice as soon as practicable after learning the person at fault was dead or not to be found` IS A BOOLEAN   -- ss 7(2), 8(6)
    `the court relieved me of the failure or gave me leave to proceed`                 IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 29A
    `I refused a medical examination without reasonable excuse and have not since had it` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 30(5)
    `a judge fixed a time to commence and it passed without my action being commenced` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 29(7)

@export Have I met the Act's conditions to bring or continue my claim for damages (ss 29, 29A, 30(5), 7(2), 7(3), 8(6))?
GIVEN `what happened` IS A `What happened to me` @desc The vehicle that hurt you and the circumstances
      `steps` IS A `My claim steps` @desc The notices you gave, any search you made, any court relief, and any refused examination or missed court deadline
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I met the conditions for my claim` IF
    CONSIDER `Whom do I claim against` `what happened`
    WHEN `no claim under this Act` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the owner or driver under the general law; this Act gives no claim on the Commission` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Insurance Commission directly, if I made due search and inquiry and gave notice (s 7(3))` THEN
        `the notices are good or relieved, and nothing bars me`
            `steps`
            (    `steps`'s `I made due search and inquiry for the vehicle as soon as practicable`
             AND `steps`'s `I gave written notice of the claim as soon as practicable after the accident`)
    WHEN `the Insurance Commission directly, for what I could have recovered from the insured person (s 7(2))` THEN
        `the notices are good or relieved, and nothing bars me`
            `steps`
            (`steps`'s `I gave notice as soon as practicable after learning the person at fault was dead or not to be found`)
    WHEN `the Insurance Commission directly, for what I could have recovered from the owner or driver (s 8(5))` THEN
        `the notices are good or relieved, and nothing bars me`
            `steps`
            (`steps`'s `I gave notice as soon as practicable after learning the person at fault was dead or not to be found`)
    OTHERWISE `the notices are good or relieved, and nothing bars me` `steps` TRUE

GIVEN `steps` IS A `My claim steps`
      `the extra notice is good` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notices are good or relieved, and nothing bars me` IF
        (   (    `steps`'s `I gave the prescribed notice of intention to claim as soon as practicable`
             AND `the extra notice is good`)
         OR `steps`'s `the court relieved me of the failure or gave me leave to proceed`)
    AND (NOT `steps`'s `I refused a medical examination without reasonable excuse and have not since had it`)
    AND (NOT `steps`'s `a judge fixed a time to commence and it passed without my action being commenced`)

-- s 29(2): if notice was given but no action commenced "within the period of 6 months after the occurrence", the Commission
-- may apply to a judge for an order that the action be commenced; (3) the claimant must be served "at least 14 days before
-- the day fixed for the hearing".
`the months before the Commission may press me to sue` MEANS 6

@export May the Insurance Commission ask a judge to order me to start my court action (s 29(2))?
GIVEN `I gave notice of intention to claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave the Commission notice of your intention to claim
      `I have commenced my action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have started your court action
      `months since the accident` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months have passed since the accident
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Commission ask a judge to order me to sue` IF
        `I gave notice of intention to claim`
    AND (NOT `I have commenced my action`)
    AND `months since the accident` AT LEAST `the months before the Commission may press me to sue`

@export At least how many days before the hearing must I be served with the Commission's application to make me sue (s 29(3))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `At least how many days before the hearing must I be served` IS 14

-- s 30(3): "The Commission must pay for an examination"; (4) the injured person "may be accompanied ... by a medical adviser
-- but not by a legal adviser".
@export May I bring my lawyer to the Insurance Commission's medical examination (s 30(4))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I bring my lawyer to the examination` IS FALSE

§§ `s 8(1), (1A), (1B), s 7(1A) -- an unpaid judgment against an uninsured owner or driver`

-- s 8(1): if the judgment debtor "does not satisfy the judgment in full within one month after the same has been entered",
-- the judgment creditor "may claim from the Commission payment of the amount (including costs) unpaid ... or the amount to
-- which the liability of the Commission might have been limited had there been in force a contract of insurance ...,
-- whichever is the smaller amount". (1A): time stayed pending appeal is excluded. (1B): for a judgment obtained in the
-- State, only if "before the action ... came on for hearing, the Commission knew that such action had been commenced".
-- The policy in the Schedule covers "all liability for negligence" with no sum stated, so no smaller limit appears in the
-- text: the claim is the unpaid amount.
@export Can I claim my unpaid judgment against an uninsured driver or owner from the Insurance Commission, and how much (s 8(1), (1A), (1B))?
GIVEN `whole months since judgment, not counting any stay pending appeal` IS A NUMBER @desc How many whole months have passed since judgment was entered, leaving out any time execution was stayed pending appeal
      `the amount unpaid` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of the judgment, with costs, is unpaid, in dollars
      `the judgment was obtained in WA` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the judgment was obtained in Western Australia
      `the Commission knew of the action before the hearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Insurance Commission knew the action had been commenced before it came on for hearing
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my unpaid judgment can I claim from the Commission` IS
    IF     `whole months since judgment, not counting any stay pending appeal` AT LEAST 1
       AND ((NOT `the judgment was obtained in WA`) OR `the Commission knew of the action before the hearing`)
    THEN `the amount unpaid`
    ELSE 0

§§ `s 12 -- emergency treatment and the trip to hospital`

-- s 12(1): for bodily injury caused by an insured or uninsured motor vehicle, where a medical practitioner or registered
-- nurse gives emergency treatment, or the injured person is "immediately after such injury conveyed in any vehicle", and the
-- practitioner, nurse or conveyor gives the Commission written notice "within one month after the occurrence", the
-- Commission "shall" pay the practitioner's or nurse's charges and travelling expenses, and the conveyor an amount under
-- the regulations (r 6: an ambulance service's agreed amount, or a formula the deposit does not reproduce).
-- s 12(3): the injured person's liability to the person paid "shall be reduced by the amount paid".
@export Will the Insurance Commission pay the doctor or nurse for my emergency treatment, so that I owe nothing (s 12(1), (3))?
GIVEN `the injury was caused by a motor vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury was directly caused by, or by the driving of, a motor vehicle (insured or uninsured)
      `the doctor or nurse gave notice within one month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the doctor or nurse gave the Commission written notice of the claim within one month of the accident
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will the Commission pay for my emergency treatment` IF
    `the injury was caused by a motor vehicle` AND `the doctor or nurse gave notice within one month`

@export How much of the emergency treatment charge is left for me to pay (s 12(3))?
GIVEN `the charge` IS A NUMBER @desc The doctor's or nurse's charge for the emergency treatment, in dollars
      `the injury was caused by a motor vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury was directly caused by, or by the driving of, a motor vehicle
      `the doctor or nurse gave notice within one month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the doctor or nurse gave the Commission written notice within one month
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of the emergency charge is left for me to pay` IS
    IF `Will the Commission pay for my emergency treatment` `the injury was caused by a motor vehicle` `the doctor or nurse gave notice within one month`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the charge`

§§ `ss 26, 27A -- waivers and legal fees`

-- s 26: "Any contract ... by virtue of which any person in advance contracts out of any right to claim damages ... in
-- respect of death or bodily injury caused or contributed to by the negligence of any other person in driving a motor
-- vehicle shall to that extent be void."
@export Have I lost my right to claim because I signed an agreement in advance not to claim for injury caused by a driver (s 26)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I signed away my right to claim` IS FALSE

-- s 27A(2): a lawyer may not agree to receive "any greater reward than is provided for by any legal costs determination"
-- under the Legal Profession Uniform Law Application Act 2022 s 133; (3) such an agreement is void and money paid under it
-- "is recoverable by the person who has paid it".
@export Is my lawyer's fee agreement for my injury claim void (s 27A)?
GIVEN `the agreed fee` IS A NUMBER @desc The fee your lawyer's agreement provides, in dollars
      `the fee the legal costs determination allows` IS A NUMBER @desc The most the legal costs determination in force provides for the work, in dollars
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my lawyer's fee agreement void` IF
    `the agreed fee` GREATER THAN `the fee the legal costs determination allows`

§§ `ss 3C, 3D, 3F, 3FB -- what damages can I get`

-- The damages rules apply to "bodily injury to a person directly caused by, or by the driving of, a motor vehicle" (ss 3A,
-- 3F(1)). The amounts in force on the date of the court's decision are used (ss 3C(13), 3D(12)); they are inputs.
DECLARE `The amounts in force` HAS
    `Amount A`  IS A NUMBER   -- s 3C: the most for non-pecuniary loss, "only in a most extreme case"
    `Amount B`  IS A NUMBER   -- s 3C: at or below it, nothing
    `Amount C`  IS A NUMBER   -- s 3C: up to it, the excess over B
    `Amount D`  IS A NUMBER   -- s 3D: at or below it, nothing for gratuitous care
    `average weekly total earnings of all employees in WA` IS A NUMBER                -- s 3D(3)(a)
    `average weekly total earnings of full-time adult employees in WA` IS A NUMBER    -- s 3F(5)(a)

-- s 3C(1): "nonpecuniary loss means -- (a) pain and suffering; (b) loss of amenities of life; (c) loss of enjoyment of life;
-- (d) curtailment of expectation of life; and (e) bodily or mental harm." (3) the maximum is Amount A; (4) assessed at
-- Amount B or less, "no damages"; (5) more than B but not more than C, "the excess of the amount so assessed over Amount B";
-- (6) more than C but less than B + C, "the excess of the amount so assessed over --" followed by a formula that is missing
-- from the deposit: NOTHING is answered for that band. At or above B + C the text makes no deduction, so the assessed
-- amount is given, not more than Amount A (the encoder's reading of (2), (3) and the bands).
@export How much can I be awarded for pain and suffering and other non-pecuniary loss (s 3C)?
GIVEN `the amounts` IS A `The amounts in force` @desc Amounts A, B, C and D and the average weekly earnings in force on the date of the decision
      `the assessed loss` IS A NUMBER @desc The court's assessment of your non-pecuniary loss, in dollars
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much for non-pecuniary loss` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the assessed loss` AT MOST `the amounts`'s `Amount B` THEN JUST 0
        IF `the assessed loss` AT MOST `the amounts`'s `Amount C` THEN JUST (`the assessed loss` MINUS `the amounts`'s `Amount B`)
        IF `the assessed loss` LESS THAN (`the amounts`'s `Amount B` PLUS `the amounts`'s `Amount C`) THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the lesser of` `the assessed loss` (`the amounts`'s `Amount A`))

-- s 3D: gratuitous domestic, nursing or attendance services by a member of the household or family. (2) nothing if they
-- "would have been or would be provided ... even if the person had not suffered the bodily injury". (3) 40 hours a week or
-- more: not more than average weekly total earnings of all WA employees, per week; (5) fewer: an hourly rate of one-fortieth
-- of that. (6) "If the amount of damages that may be awarded under subsection (3) or (5) is Amount D or less, no damages".
-- Read here as the value assessed, held to the cap, compared with Amount D.
@export How much can I be awarded for care my family gives me without charge (s 3D)?
GIVEN `the amounts` IS A `The amounts in force` @desc Amounts A, B, C and D and the average weekly earnings
      `the care would have been given anyway` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the care would have been given even without the injury
      `hours of care a week` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours a week the care is given
      `weeks of care` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks
      `the value assessed` IS A NUMBER @desc The court's valuation of the care, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much for gratuitous care` IS
    IF `the care would have been given anyway` OR `held to the cap` AT MOST `the amounts`'s `Amount D`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `held to the cap`
    WHERE
        `the weekly rate` MEANS `the amounts`'s `average weekly total earnings of all employees in WA`
        `the cap` MEANS
            IF `hours of care a week` AT LEAST 40
            THEN `the weekly rate` TIMES `weeks of care`
            ELSE (`the weekly rate` DIVIDED BY 40) TIMES `hours of care a week` TIMES `weeks of care`
        `held to the cap` MEANS `the lesser of` `the value assessed` `the cap`

-- s 3F(4): earning capacity "is to be disregarded to the extent that it would have exceeded a capacity to earn 3 times the
-- average weekly earnings at the date of the award"; (5) the full-time adult WA figure.
@export What weekly earning capacity can count towards my damages for lost earnings (s 3F)?
GIVEN `the amounts` IS A `The amounts in force` @desc The average weekly earnings at the date of the award
      `my weekly earning capacity` IS A NUMBER @desc What you could have earned a week but for the injury, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What weekly earning capacity counts` IS
    `the lesser of` `my weekly earning capacity` (3 TIMES `the amounts`'s `average weekly total earnings of full-time adult employees in WA`)

-- s 3FB(3): for damages for treatment, care and support needs of a catastrophic injury, "no deduction is to be made for any
-- contributory negligence of the person".
@export Can my damages for the care of a catastrophic injury be cut because I was partly to blame (s 3FB)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my catastrophic care damages be cut for my own fault` IS FALSE
